  "overview": {
    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Hilda Solis is the Chair of the Los Angeles County Board of Supervisors and a former U.S. Secretary of Labor who previously served in the state Assembly, state Senate, and U.S. House. She identifies housing, groceries, childcare, and healthcare as components of the district's biggest challenge: a cost of living that has outpaced wages. She has proposed rolling back tariffs and prioritizing tax relief for working families, and supports comprehensive immigration reform with a permanent pathway to citizenship. She authored a Board of Supervisors motion opposing proposed U.S. Census changes that would exclude certain immigrants from the count used to apportion House seats. She said she would support reversing cuts to Medicare and Medicaid and wants to expand Medicare's ability to negotiate drug prices.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3, 4],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Hilda Solis is the Chair of the Los Angeles County Board of Supervisors and a former U.S. Secretary of Labor who previously served in the state Assembly, state Senate, and U.S. House.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She identifies housing, groceries, childcare, and healthcare as components of the district's biggest challenge: a cost of living that has outpaced wages.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She has proposed rolling back tariffs and prioritizing tax relief for working families, and supports comprehensive immigration reform with a permanent pathway to citizenship.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "She authored a Board of Supervisors motion opposing proposed U.S. Census changes that would exclude certain immigrants from the count used to apportion House seats.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "She said she would support reversing cuts to Medicare and Medicaid and wants to expand Medicare's ability to negotiate drug prices.",
            "cites": [4]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "As supervisor, she hosted the opening of three new behavioral health facilities at the Restorative Care Village, including a psychiatric facility, a withdrawal management facility, and a 24-hour mental health urgent care center. She also moved to ban AI hyperscale data centers in unincorporated county areas, citing concerns about public health and environmental protections. She announced an additional $250,000 investment to distribute health-code-compliant food carts to street vendors, bringing the county's total program investment to $1.78 million. Her official website states she convened county departments for a recovery update following a major warehouse fire and opposed the warehouse operator's permit application to rebuild. She joined officials to break ground on 202 affordable homes on the site of a former children's center.",
        "cites": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9],
        "sentences": [
